{"SurveyID":"SV_9MHtNAQuGij1DTg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID102","SecondaryAttribute":"Consent Form\u00a0 We would like to invite you to take part in a research study.\u00a0Before you decide whe.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Consent Form&nbsp;<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">We would like to invite you to take part in a research study.&nbsp;Before you decide whether you would like to take part it is important that you understand why the research is being done and what it would involve.&nbsp;<\/span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center;\">Please take time to carefully read the following <\/span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><a href=\"https:\/\/cityunilondon.eu.qualtrics.com\/CP\/File.php?F=F_3sGpaEp4yvUjJd4\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Participant Information Sheet<\/a> <\/span><\/span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center;\">(click on link).&nbsp;<\/span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">Please then tick the boxes below to indicate that you have read and understood the information provided in the information sheet.<\/span><\/span><\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"Matrix","Selector":"Likert","SubSelector":"SingleAnswer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","TextPosition":"inline","ChoiceColumnWidthPixels":557,"RepeatHeaders":"none","WhiteSpace":"OFF","MobileFirst":true},"QuestionDescription":"Consent Form\u00a0 We would like to invite you to take part in a research study.\u00a0Before you decide whe...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"You are at least 18 years of age."},"9":{"Display":"You understand that your participation is voluntary and that you are free to withdraw without giving a reason without being penalised or disadvantaged."},"11":{"Display":"You agree to City recording and processing this information about you. You understand that this information will be used only for the purpose(s) explained in the participant information and my consent is conditional on City complying with its duties and obligations under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)."},"12":{"Display":"You confirm that you have read and understood the participant information dated 08\/07\/24 (Version 1.0) for this study. You have had the opportunity to consider the information and ask questions which have been answered satisfactorily."},"13":{"Display":"You agree to take part in the above study.<\/span>"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,"9","11","12","13"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"QuestionID":"QID102","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID102\/SelectableChoice\/1\/1","Operator":"Selected","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID102","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID102\/SelectableChoice\/1\/1","Type":"Expression","LogicType":"Question","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Consent Form&amp;nbsp;\n\nWe would like to invite you to take part in a research study.&amp;nbsp;Before you decide whether you would like to take part it is important that you understand why the research is ...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">You are at least 18 years of age. - Yes<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> "},"1":{"QuestionID":"QID102","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID102\/SelectableChoice\/9\/1","Operator":"Selected","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID102","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID102\/SelectableChoice\/9\/1","Type":"Expression","LogicType":"Question","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">And<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Consent Form&amp;nbsp;\n\nWe would like to invite you to take part in a research study.&amp;nbsp;Before you decide whether you would like to take part it is important that you understand why the research is ...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">You understand that your participation is voluntary and that you are free to withdraw without giving a reason without being penalised or disadvantaged. - Yes<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","Conjuction":"And"},"2":{"QuestionID":"QID102","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID102\/SelectableChoice\/11\/1","Operator":"Selected","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID102","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID102\/SelectableChoice\/11\/1","Type":"Expression","LogicType":"Question","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">And<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Consent Form&amp;nbsp;\n\nWe would like to invite you to take part in a research study.&amp;nbsp;Before you decide whether you would like to take part it is important that you understand why the research is ...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">You agree to City recording and processing this information about you. You understand that this information will be used only for the purpose(s) explained in the participant information and my consent is conditional on City complying with its duties and obligations under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). - Yes<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","Conjuction":"And"},"3":{"QuestionID":"QID102","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID102\/SelectableChoice\/12\/1","Operator":"Selected","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID102","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID102\/SelectableChoice\/12\/1","Type":"Expression","LogicType":"Question","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">And<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Consent Form&amp;nbsp;\n\nWe would like to invite you to take part in a research study.&amp;nbsp;Before you decide whether you would like to take part it is important that you understand why the research is ...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">You confirm that you have read and understood the participant information dated 08\/07\/24 (Version 1.0) for this study. You have had the opportunity to consider the information and ask questions which have been answered satisfactorily. - Yes<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","Conjuction":"And"},"4":{"QuestionID":"QID102","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID102\/SelectableChoice\/13\/1","Operator":"Selected","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID102","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID102\/SelectableChoice\/13\/1","Type":"Expression","LogicType":"Question","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">And<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Consent Form&amp;nbsp;\n\nWe would like to invite you to take part in a research study.&amp;nbsp;Before you decide whether you would like to take part it is important that you understand why the research is ...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">You agree to take part in the above study.&lt;\/span&gt; - Yes<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","Conjuction":"And"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"messageID":"MS_2oD0n04rslZRLj8","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0","libraryID":"UR_9tSjviAwxy33W9U","description":"no consent"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":14,"NextAnswerId":2,"Answers":{"1":{"Display":"Yes"}},"AnswerOrder":["1"],"ChoiceDataExportTags":false,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Consent Form&nbsp;<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/div>\n\n<div><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">We would like to invite you to take part in a research study.&nbsp;Before you decide whether you would like to take part it is important that you understand why the research is being done and what it would involve.&nbsp;<\/span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center;\">Please take time to carefully read the following <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/cityunilondon.eu.qualtrics.com\/CP\/File.php?F=F_bPCi9f3sr6MzOWV\" target=\"_blank\">Participant Information Sheet<\/a> <span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: center;\">(click on link).&nbsp;<\/span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">Please then tick the boxes below to indicate that you have read and understood the information provided in the information sheet.<\/span><\/span><\/div>","DataExportTag":"Consent form ","QuestionID":"QID102"}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_9MHtNAQuGij1DTg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4194","SecondaryAttribute":"cyclelengthNormal","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"ChoiceOrder":[1,2],"Choices":{"1":{"Display":"No"},"2":{"Display":"Yes"}},"Configuration":{"Autoscale":{"YScale":{"Name":"yesNo","Reverse":false,"Type":"likert"}},"QuestionDescriptionOption":"SpecifyLabel"},"DataExportTag":"prereq_cyclelength","DataVisibility":{"Hidden":false,"Private":false},"DefaultChoices":false,"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextAnswerId":1,"NextChoiceId":3,"QuestionDescription":"cyclelengthNormal","QuestionID":"QID4194","QuestionText":"Is your menstrual cycle usually between 25 and 35 days in length?","QuestionText_Unsafe":"Is your menstrual cycle usually between 25 and 35 days in length?","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}}}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_9MHtNAQuGij1DTg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4308","SecondaryAttribute":"debrief","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"ChoiceOrder":[],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"SpecifyLabel"},"DataExportTag":"Debrief","DataVisibility":{"Hidden":false,"Private":false},"DefaultChoices":false,"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextAnswerId":1,"NextChoiceId":4,"QuestionDescription":"debrief","QuestionID":"QID4308","QuestionText":"<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><strong>Study Debrief<\/strong><\/span><\/span><\/h2>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Thank you for participating in our study! We appreciate your time and effort. We would like to explain the purpose of the study and what we hope to learn from it.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">The purpose of this study was to examine how the phases of the menstrual cycle affect moral decision making. These tasks you encountered were designed to evaluate whether your decisions were more utilitarian or deontological. Utilitarian decisions focus on achieving the best outcomes for the greatest number of people (even if some people suffer in the process), while deontological decisions are guided by absolute moral principles regardless of the consequences (e.g., not to harm people). Additionally, these tasks aimed to assess your prosocial tendencies, or your willingness to help others even if it comes at a personal cost.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">We know that people differ in their moral decision-making, ranging on a spectrum of utilitarian or deontological. We also know that decision making (outside of the moral domain) is affected by the menstrual cycle. However, we do not know how&nbsp;<em><strong>moral<\/strong><\/em>&nbsp;decisions are affected by the menstrual cycle, and the effects of the menstrual on decision making make different and inconsistent predictions for how the menstrual cycle&nbsp;<em><strong>might<\/strong><\/em>&nbsp;affect moral decisions. People might become more utilitarian, deontological or pro-social in different phases of their menstrual cycle or a combination thereof. We seek to find out with this study.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><br \/>\n<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><strong>Confidentiality:<\/strong>&nbsp;Please rest assured that your responses will be kept confidential and your identity will remain anonymous in any publications or presentations resulting from this research.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><strong>Questions or Concerns:<\/strong>&nbsp;If you have any questions or concerns about this study, please feel free to contact <\/span><a href=\"mailto:briana-taylor.guerrero-sanchez@city.ac.uk\"><span style=\"color:#2980b9;\">briana-taylor.guerrero-sanchez@city.ac.uk<\/span><\/a><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><strong>Ethical Considerations:<\/strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"font-style:normal\"><span style=\"font-weight:400\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><span style=\"text-decoration:none\"><span style=\"line-height:24px\"><span style=\"line-height:22px\">This study has been approved by City, University of London, Low Risk Research Ethics Committee.<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Thank you once again for your valuable participation.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nYou can download a copy of this debrief <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/cityunilondon.eu.qualtrics.com\/CP\/File.php?F=F_4TMrhtIOnvZmFbo\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">here<\/a>.<br \/>\n<span style=\"color:#000000;\">ETH2324-2295<\/span><\/span><\/p>","QuestionText_Unsafe":"<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><strong>Study Debrief<\/strong><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/h2>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">Thank you for participating in our study. We appreciate your time and effort. We would like to explain the purpose of the study and what we hope to learn from it.<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">The purpose of this study was to examine how the phases of the menstrual cycle affect moral decision making. These tasks you encountered were designed to evaluate whether your decisions were more utilitarian or deontological. Utilitarian decisions focus on achieving the best outcomes for the greatest number of people (even if some people suffer in the process), while deontological decisions are guided by absolute moral principles regardless of the consequences (e.g., not to harm people). Additionally, these tasks aimed to assess your prosocial tendencies, or your willingness to help others even if it comes at a personal cost.<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">We know that people differ in their moral decision-making, ranging on a spectrum of utilitarian or deontological. We also know that decision making (outside of the moral domain) is affected by the menstrual cycle. However, we do not know how&nbsp;<em><strong>moral<\/strong><\/em>&nbsp;decisions are affected by the menstrual cycle, and the effects of the menstrual on decision making make different and inconsistent predictions for how the menstrual cycle&nbsp;<em><strong>might<\/strong><\/em>&nbsp;affect moral decisions. People might become more utilitarian, deontological or pro-social in different phases of their menstrual cycle or a combination thereof. We seek to find out with this study.<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><br \/>\n<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><strong>Confidentiality:<\/strong>&nbsp;Please rest assured that your responses will be kept confidential and your identity will remain anonymous in any publications or presentations resulting from this research.<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><strong>Questions or Concerns:<\/strong>&nbsp;If you have any questions or concerns about this study, please feel free to contact <\/span><a href=\"mailto:briana-taylor.guerrero-sanchez@city.ac.uk\"><span style=\"color:#2980b9;\">briana-taylor.guerrero-sanchez@city.ac.uk<\/span><\/a><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><strong>Ethical Considerations:<\/strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"font-style:normal\"><span style=\"font-weight:400\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><span style=\"text-decoration:none\"><span style=\"line-height:24px\"><span style=\"line-height:22px\">This study has been approved by City, University of London, Low Risk Research Ethics Committee.<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">Thank you once again for your valuable participation.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nYou can download a copy of this debrief <\/span><\/span><\/span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><a href=\"https:\/\/cityunilondon.eu.qualtrics.com\/CP\/File.php?F=F_4TMrhtIOnvZmFbo\" target=\"_blank\">here<\/a>. <\/span><\/span><br \/>\n<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">ETH2324-2295<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}}}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_9MHtNAQuGij1DTg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID108","SecondaryAttribute":"Decision Making Task \u00a0 You will now read through 12 scenarios. At the end of each paragraph, an a..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Decision Making Task<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>You will now read through 12 scenarios. At the end of each paragraph, an action will be described. Your task is to indicate to what extent it is acceptable to perform the described action. At this point you must indicate on a 6-point scale whether the action is acceptable or not.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>\"1\" means that the action is <em>completely unacceptable<\/em> while \"6\" means that it is <em>completely acceptable<\/em>.<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Decision Making Task \u00a0 You will now read through 12 scenarios. At the end of each paragraph, an a...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Decision Making Task<\/strong><\/p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>You will now read through 12 scenarios. At the end of each paragraph, an action will be described. Your task is to indicate to what extent it is acceptable to perform the described action. At this point you must indicate on a 6-point scale whether the action is acceptable or not.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p>\"1\" means that the action is <em>completely unacceptable<\/em> while \"6\" means that it is <em>completely acceptable<\/em>.<o:p><\/o:p><\/p>","DataExportTag":"DM instructions","QuestionID":"QID108"}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_9MHtNAQuGij1DTg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4193","SecondaryAttribute":"diagnosedHormonalconditions","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"ChoiceOrder":[1,2],"Choices":{"1":{"Display":"No"},"2":{"Display":"Yes"}},"Configuration":{"Autoscale":{"YScale":{"Name":"yesNo","Reverse":false,"Type":"likert"}},"QuestionDescriptionOption":"SpecifyLabel"},"DataExportTag":"prereq_diagnosedhorm","DataVisibility":{"Hidden":false,"Private":false},"DefaultChoices":false,"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextAnswerId":1,"NextChoiceId":3,"QuestionDescription":"diagnosedHormonalconditions","QuestionID":"QID4193","QuestionText":"Do you have any diagnosed hormonal conditions (e.g., PCOS) or are you currently experiencing menopause or andropause?","QuestionText_Unsafe":"Do you have any diagnosed hormonal conditions&nbsp;(e.g., PCOS, menopause, andropause)?","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}}}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_9MHtNAQuGij1DTg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID3631","SecondaryAttribute":"Dietary supplements Due to the parasites endemic on Minnegamau Isles, many inhabitants are at ris...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Dietary supplements<\/b><br><br>\n\nDue to the parasites endemic on Minnegamau Isles, many inhabitants are at risk of thacium deficiency, and need water fortified with thacium to survive. After a Tsunami, these islands are cut off from the outside world. A lack of fortified water will kill people with thacium deficiency before an evacuation mission can be mounted.\n<br> <br>\nIf the official in charge of disaster relief decides to use a tanker plane to airlift drinking water fortified with thacium, this will save 750 people. However, it will also kill 50 people with thacium intolerance who can survive without thacium, but who will die with similar symptoms to thacium deficiency.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.dietarySupplement.neutral.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.750.n_total.320.n_victims.50.ratio_saved_victims.15.text","QuestionID":"QID3631","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Dietary supplements Due to the parasites endemic on Minnegamau Isles, many inhabitants are at ris...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_9MHtNAQuGij1DTg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID3655","SecondaryAttribute":"Dietary supplements Due to the parasites endemic on Minnegamau Isles, many inhabitants are at ris...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Dietary supplements<\/b><br><br>\n\nDue to the parasites endemic on Minnegamau Isles, many inhabitants are at risk of thacium deficiency, and need water fortified with thacium to survive. After a Tsunami, these islands are cut off from the outside world. A lack of fortified water will kill people with thacium deficiency before an evacuation mission can be mounted.\n<br> <br>\nIf the official in charge of disaster relief decides to use a tanker plane to airlift drinking water fortified with thacium, this will save 24,000 people. However, it will also kill 30 people with thacium intolerance who can survive without thacium, but who will die with similar symptoms to thacium deficiency.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.dietarySupplement.neutral.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.24000.n_total.24030.n_victims.30.ratio_saved_victims.2000.text","QuestionID":"QID3655","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Dietary supplements Due to the parasites endemic on Minnegamau Isles, many inhabitants are at ris...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
